<title>CANADA: Uniforet unit plans groundwood downtime.</title>
<headline>Uniforet unit plans groundwood downtime.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tripap Inc, a 65 percent owned unit of Uniforet Inc said on Wednesday that it plans to take temporary downtime at its mill in Trois-Rivieres, Quebec because of soft seasonal conditions.</p>
<p>The shutdown, planned for December 21 to January 6, represents about 5,200 metric tons of uncoated groundwood. Tripap will continue to ship orders during the period, the company said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
